body:
@Mic92 Thanks! I updated the kernel in the CentOS virtual machine to 5.0.11 but the error still persists. I checked, and the /lib directory is there.

I understand you lack of motivation. What I could do to facilitate your work in this direction is to create a CentOS VPS say, on Hetzner or Digital Ocean (for which I would pay) and make it available to you. I am very keen on seeing this run on CentOS because nix is a very good candidate to be used on clusters where one does not have root access, and most clusters I know (In academia, where I work) use RHEL or CentOS.

However, I understand that you might not be motivated to work on this and I thank you for all the effort you have already undertook.

@valmar could you also create a regular file in / and see if it gets bind mounted properly into the chroot?

for example:

```
$ echo foo > /test
```

@DavHau what is your opinion on this, since you already maintain https://github.com/DavHau/nix-portable
I am missing a bit of a usecase for nix-user-chroot, which is why it does not has a high priority for me personally.
But I also see how it can be useful for others so I am not so sure how to move forward with the project.

@rrbutani the functionality that you are describing make sense to have but I feel like it's turning a bit into what bubblewrap already provide to us. However I also see that value in just having one binary that is easy to install. So I am a bit unsure.
